<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss Life sells La Suiza Spanish unit.</title>
<headline>Swiss Life sells La Suiza Spanish unit.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Life/Rentenanstalt said it was selling its La Suiza Insurances subsidiary in Barcelona to the British insurance company Eagle Star.</p>
<p>Separately, the company said it will increase the share capital of its Swiss Life (Espana) unit in Madrid to 3,500 million pesetas from 1,800 million.</p>
<p>Swiss Life provided no details on the La  Suiza sale transaction. But it said La Suiza is mainly active in the area of non-life insurance and it earned premiums of approximately 110 million Swiss francs in 1996.</p>
<p>The sale is in keeping with its strategy of limiting business activities mainly to personal insurance, Swiss Life also said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
